import{_ as n,o as t,c as i,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 784 | Transcended Ones and Institutions · Overview — The Transcended One's Position Within Civilizational Institutions","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 784 | Transcended Ones and Institutions · Overview — The Transcended One's Position Within Civilizational Institutions","no":784,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Institutions","Overview","Anchor Symbiosis","Governance Framework"],"related":["40-Symbiotic Constitution General Outline","49-Governance Framework and Checks-and-Balances","701-Transcendence-Orthodox Definition Overview"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0784_模块4-制度-总论.md","filePath":"en/0784_模块4-制度-总论.md"}`),s={name:"en/0784_模块4-制度-总论.md"};function a(r,e,l,h,d,u){return t(),i("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-784-transcended-ones-and-institutions-·-overview-—-the-transcended-one-s-position-within-civilizational-institutions" tabindex="-1">Entry 784 | Transcended Ones and Institutions · Overview — The Transcended One&#39;s Position Within Civilizational Institutions <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-784-transcended-ones-and-institutions-·-overview-—-the-transcended-one-s-position-within-civilizational-institutions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 784 | Transcended Ones and Institutions · Overview — The Transcended One&#39;s Position Within Civilizational Institutions&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 40, 49, 701</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-the-strongest-person-stands-on-which-side-of-institutions" tabindex="-1">Introduction: the strongest person stands on which side of institutions? <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-the-strongest-person-stands-on-which-side-of-institutions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: the strongest person stands on which side of institutions?&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old world&#39;s transcended ones are always above institutions. Heavenly Emperors do not obey law; Immortal Emperors do not follow rules; cosmos overlords do not enter courts — he is already strongest, institutions cannot reach him. Heng Yuan Zhou must squarely answer: <strong>one person strong enough for the Balanced Anchor Hyper-Multiverse Realm — in the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s institutions, on what position does he actually stand?</strong> This entry, as this group&#39;s overview, must pin this position down. The answer: <strong>he does not stand above institutions; he stands within them.</strong></p><p>Six top-level axioms all line up: the anti-predation axiom requires the institutional position contain no predation; the republican axiom of Myriad Races requires institutions apply equally to transcended ones and Myriad Ranks; the collective ascension axiom requires the institutional position serve common uplift; the causal self-discipline axiom requires the institutional position not create causal loopholes; the law-first axiom requires the institutional position be self-consistent at the law layer, not rewritable by any transcended individual.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-the-old-world-s-three-outside-institution-positions" tabindex="-1">I. The Old World&#39;s Three &quot;Outside-Institution&quot; Positions <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-the-old-world-s-three-outside-institution-positions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. The Old World&#39;s Three &quot;Outside-Institution&quot; Positions&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old world&#39;s transcended-one/institution relationship, no matter how varied, always falls on three:</p><ol><li><strong>Above institutions</strong>: the transcended one is institutions themselves; his word is law. Representatives: Shi Hao, various Heavenly Emperors;</li><li><strong>Outside institutions</strong>: the transcended one has transcended institutions; institutions cannot reach him. Representatives: Ji-Ning-style closed-door retirement;</li><li><strong>Within institutions but privileged</strong>: the transcended one ostensibly obeys law, but institutions open back doors for him. Representatives: various &quot;protagonist&#39;s law-granted mercy.&quot;</li></ol><p>Three positions look different, but their essence is the same — <strong>the transcended one and ordinary people are not on the same legal line.</strong> Institutions for him either do not exist, or are his tool.</p><h2 id="ii-heng-yuan-zhou-s-new-position-within-institutions-equal-application" tabindex="-1">II. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s New Position: Within Institutions, Equal Application <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-heng-yuan-zhou-s-new-position-within-institutions-equal-application" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s New Position: Within Institutions, Equal Application&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s new position abolishes all three old positions:</p><blockquote><p><strong>The transcended one is within institutions, subject to the same law as all Myriad-Rank beings. He has no extra-legal privilege, no institutional immunity; every bit of his power is institutionally granted and institutionally revocable.</strong></p></blockquote><p>This new position has three components:</p><ul><li><strong>Same law</strong>: the transcended one violating Myriad-Rank law goes through the same procedure and receives the same sanction as any Myriad-Rank being. No &quot;transcended-one amnesty&quot; exists;</li><li><strong>Same responsibility</strong>: causal damage caused by the transcended one is borne by himself; &quot;I did it for your own good&quot; may not offset it;</li><li><strong>Same vote</strong>: the transcended one has only one vote in the Anchor Council, equal to Myriad-Rank representatives. His &quot;strength&quot; gives him no extra power.</li></ul><p>Three components stack, turning the transcended one from a &quot;superman outside institutions&quot; into a &quot;citizen within institutions&quot; — a citizen who happens to have 10,000 times the computable power.</p><h2 id="iii-institutional-position-s-three-consequences" tabindex="-1">III. Institutional Position&#39;s Three Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-institutional-position-s-three-consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Institutional Position&#39;s Three Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Placing the transcended one within institutions produces three hard consequences:</p><ol><li><strong>The transcended one cannot make law</strong>: he may propose, but cannot legislate himself. Legislative power rests with the Anchor Council;</li><li><strong>The transcended one cannot break law</strong>: if he breaks law, the Symbiotic Court hears him, with no &quot;strength immunity&quot;;</li><li><strong>The transcended one cannot abolish law</strong>: he cannot abolish a law because it is &quot;inconvenient.&quot; Law revision goes through Anchor Council procedure.</li></ol><p>Three consequences ensure institutions are always Myriad Ranks&#39; public tool, not the transcended one&#39;s private toy.</p><h2 id="iv-six-sub-articles-positioning-preview" tabindex="-1">IV. Six Sub-Articles&#39; Positioning Preview <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-six-sub-articles-positioning-preview" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Six Sub-Articles&#39; Positioning Preview&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Entries 785–790, six sub-articles, will handle the transcended one&#39;s relationship with four institutional bodies, plus two cross-cutting questions:</p><ul><li><strong>Anchor Council</strong> (785): what role does the transcended one play in the legislative body?</li><li><strong>Symbiotic Executive Committee</strong> (786): what role does the transcended one play in the administrative body?</li><li><strong>Symbiotic Court</strong> (787): what role does the transcended one play in the judicial body?</li><li><strong>Anchor Supervisory Committee</strong> (788): what role does the transcended one play in the supervisory body?</li><li><strong>Legal Constraints and Immunity Boundaries</strong> (789): does the transcended one have any legal immunity? Where is the immunity boundary?</li><li><strong>Checks-and-Balances Mechanism</strong> (790): how do the four bodies check each other, ensuring the transcended one does not turn any body into a private tool?</li></ul><p>Six dimensions together are the complete organizational chart of &quot;transcended one within institutions.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: the old world letting the strongest be outside institutions equals letting institutions lose their strongest executor; Heng Yuan Zhou pulls the transcended one into institutions, letting his computable power serve institutional operation</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: the transcended one outside institutions is naturally a predator — he has no constraint; the transcended one within institutions must obey law, predatory paths sealed</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo is &quot;institutions themselves&quot; in his plane; Heng Yuan Zhou requires the transcended one be only one post within institutions</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: institutions apply equally to all Myriad-Rank beings; the transcended one may not be an exception</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: all rules of the transcended-one/institution relationship are opened network-wide through the Selfless Dao; Myriad Ranks may inspect. The transcended one&#39;s every step in institutions is recorded by Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision; civilizational weight real-time reflects his in-institution performance</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The strongest person stands within institutions, not above them. This is not disparagement of the transcended one, but respect for institutions — a good institution should be able to manage anyone, including the strongest. If an institution cannot manage the strongest, then it is not an institution, but a yoke for the weak. Heng Yuan Zhou does not want that kind of yoke; Heng Yuan Zhou wants a cage that even the transcended one must enter.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/40-共生宪法总纲.html">Entry 40 · Symbiotic Constitution General Outline</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/49-治理框架与权力制衡.html">Entry 49 · Governance Framework and Checks-and-Balances</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/701-超脱正统定义总论.html">Entry 701 · Transcendence-Orthodox Definition Overview</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/780_模块4-万族-超脱者的监督机制.html">Entry 780 · Transcended One&#39;s Supervision Mechanism</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const g=n(s,[["render",a]]);export{p as __pageData,g as default};
